[center][size=6][b]EMBERVALE TELEPORT[/b][/size]
[size=4][color=#e8c882]M A P   B A S E D   T E L E P O R T[/color][/size]

[size=3]Point at the map. Hold. You're there.[/size][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/219/219-1792774481-2009229754.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]

Open the world map, hold [b]Shift[/b] and hold the [b]left mouse button[/b] on any spot for one second. The map closes and you travel there.
[list]
[*][b]The game's own teleport[/b]: the native travel animation and effect, not a jerky position hack.
[*][b]Lands you on the ground[/b] at the spot you picked, not inside a hill or high in the air.
[*][b]Waits for unloaded terrain[/b]: far-away land is loaded first, so the height is never guessed.
[*][b]Hard to trigger by accident[/b]: a ring around the cursor fills while you hold. Let go early, press Esc or right-click to cancel.
[*][b]Short notices[/b] ("Teleporting in 3...") tell you what is happening.
[*][b]In your language:[/b] the notices follow the game's language setting, in all 15 languages Enshrouded supports.
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/219/219-1792774481-750098283.jpg[/img]

[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/219/219-1792774485-1759040260.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Close Enshrouded.
[*]Open the game folder (Steam: right-click Enshrouded > Manage > Browse local files).
[*]Copy everything from the zip into it, keeping the folders: [b]dbgcore.dll[/b] next to [i]enshrouded.exe[/i], and the [b]greeneye\map-teleport[/b] folder.
[*]Start the game, open the map, hold [b]Shift[/b] and hold the left mouse button on a spot.
[/list]

[b]Single player and hosting your own game:[/b] that's all. Your game is the host.

[b]Install by hand:[/b] Vortex does not know the Greeneye Loader yet.

[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete [i]greeneye\map-teleport[/i]; if no other Greeneye mod is left, also [i]dbgcore.dll[/i] and the [i]greeneye[/i] folder.

[line]

[size=4][b]Dedicated server[/b][/size]

On a dedicated server the mod has to be on the server [b]and[/b] on the game of every player who wants to teleport.
[list=1]
[*]Stop the server.
[*]Open the server folder, the one with [i]enshrouded_server.exe[/i]. In Steam: Library > Tools > Enshrouded Dedicated Server > right-click > Manage > Browse local files. With SteamCMD it's the folder you installed to; with a rented server, use the host's file manager or FTP.
[*]Copy everything from the zip into that folder, the same way as for the game: [b]dbgcore.dll[/b] next to [i]enshrouded_server.exe[/i], and the [b]greeneye\map-teleport[/b] folder.
[*]Start the server.
[*]Check it loaded: [i]greeneye\loader.log[/i] in the server folder should contain [i]Embervale Teleport 1.1.2: server companion loaded[/i].
[/list]

[b]Players:[/b] each player installs the mod on their own game as described above. Players without the mod can still join and play; they just can't teleport, and they won't see anything from the mod.

[b]Settings:[/b] the server's own [i]map-teleport.ini[/i] decides how teleports behave for everyone on that server. Each player's own ini only decides whether, and in which language, their notices are shown.

[b]Rented servers:[/b] the host must let you add files next to [i]enshrouded_server.exe[/i]. Tested on a Windows server; not tested on Linux/Wine hosting.

[line]

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]

More settings are in [i]greeneye\map-teleport\map-teleport.ini[/i], each explained in the file. For example, arrive high above the spot and glide down, or hide the mod's notices. Restart the game (or the server) after changing it.

[line]

[size=4][b]Languages[/b][/size]

The notices come in every language the game supports: English, French, Italian, German, Spanish, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Portuguese (Brazil), Russian, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Turkish, Ukrainian and Thai. They follow the language set in the game, also when you change it while playing. To pick one yourself, set [i]Language[/i] in the ini.

The translations were made with AI. If a line reads oddly in your language, please post a better one in the comments.

[line]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Single player, hosting your own game, and dedicated servers[/b] (install it on the server too). Players without the mod can share the server and notice nothing.
[*]On a server without the mod, map teleport is simply unavailable: Shift + hold tells you so, and nothing shows up in chat.
[*][b]Plays well with other mods.[/b] It runs through the Greeneye Loader ([i]dbgcore.dll[/i], shared with Find, Quick Deposit and Continue), and where another mod such as Creative Mode hooks the same game function, it chains onto that hook.
[*][b]Safe on game updates.[/b] Made for the current game version. After an update the mod checks that it still recognises the game; if it does not, it switches itself off instead of risking a crash.
[*]Works with Steam. Not tested with other store versions.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

If something doesn't work, please post this file with your report:
[list]
[*][i]greeneye\loader.log[/i] in the game folder: what the Greeneye Loader and the mod did (the mod's lines start with "Map Teleport:").
[*]On a dedicated server, also [i]greeneye\loader.log[/i] from the server folder.
[/list]

[line]

